2. What it does not cover: the trained model and the label list

These files carry upstream terms and are not relicensed by the MIT licence:

  - crop_disease.onnx
  - class_names.json
  - model_metrics.json

The model was trained on PlantVillage images. PlantVillage is published under
two different terms depending on which release was downloaded. The original
2015 release announcement states CC BY-SA 3.0 and adds that algorithms trained
on the data fall under the same licence. The GitHub repository and the common
Kaggle mirrors are listed as CC0 1.0. These two do not agree.

If this project was trained from a CC BY-SA release, then the model is
arguably CC BY-SA as well and must be shared under the same terms. If it came
from a CC0 mirror, there is no such condition. The exact provenance of the
copy used here has not been settled. Anyone redistributing the model
commercially should resolve this first.

See the "Data, licences and credits" section of README.md for full citations.


3. Benchmark data, not training data

PlantDoc was used as a benchmark only, to measure how the model performs on
real field photos. It was not used as training data for the shipped model.
PlantDoc is published under CC BY 4.0, attribution required, no share-alike.
Citation: Singh, D., Jain, N., Jain, P., Kayal, P., Kumawat, S., & Batra, N.
(2020). PlantDoc: A Dataset for Visual Plant Disease Detection. CoDS-COMAD
2020, 249-253. doi:10.1145/3371158.3371196


4. Third-party libraries

PyTorch and torchvision are BSD-3-Clause. MobileNetV3 ImageNet weights are
BSD-3-Clause. ONNX Runtime, Gradio, NumPy and the remaining dependencies keep
their own licences. The full table is in README.md.


5. No warranty on agricultural advice

The treatment suggestions, cost estimates and severity notes in this project
are illustrative decision support, not agronomic advice. They are not a
substitute for a KVK or an agriculture officer. The model is a closed-set
classifier trained on laboratory photographs and it can be wrong, including
confidently wrong, on real field photographs. Do not rely on it as the only
basis for a spraying or spending decision.